"CHGP Tops Out Ayanna Resort Residences in Bukit Jalil, Targets Q2 2027 Handover - Chin Hin Group Property (https://chinhinproperty.com/blog/chgp-ayanna-resort-residences-bukit-jalil-handover/)\nciteturn371search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; KUALA LUMPUR, 28 AUGUST 2026 — Chin Hin Group Property (“CHGP”) has officially marked a major milestone in its residential portfolio with the successful topping out of Ayanna Resort Residences in Jalan Mas, Bukit Jalil. ... Following the completion of structural works, construction focus now shifts to architectural façade installation, exterior envelope finishing, electrical and mechanical (M&E) fittings, and interior unit fit-outs.\n\nCHGP Tops Out Ayanna Resort Residences in Bukit Jalil, Targets Q2 2027 Handover\n\nAugust 28, 2026\n\nImage: 001.png\n\nKUALA LUMPUR, 28 AUGUST 2026 — Chin Hin Group Property (“CHGP”) has officially marked a major milestone in its residential portfolio with the successful topping out of Ayanna Resort Residences in Jalan Mas, Bukit Jalil. The structural completion of the project’s residential towers signals the transition into the final stages of construction, keeping the project firmly on track for handover in Q2 2027.\nSpanning two high-rise towers across 4.9 acres of freehold land—Block A (42 storeys, 333 units) and Block B (44 storeys, 491 units)—Ayanna Resort Residences comprises 824 units designed for modern, multi-generational living.\nThe development has achieved a stellar 95% take-up rate prior to reaching its structural peak, reflecting strong market confidence and sustained demand for thoughtfully designed homes. In addition, this award-winning project has also earned the GreenRE Certification in recognition of its energy-efficient, environmentally sustainable design and green building practices, meeting the expectations of today's sustainability-conscious homebuyers.\nWith a Gross Development Value (GDV) of RM732.1 million, the project reinforces its position as a standout premium residential offering in the market.\nReflecting on the milestone, CHGP Executive Director Chang Tze Yoong said, \"Reaching the structural topping-out milestone of Ayanna Resort Residences marks a pivotal chapter for Chin Hin Group Property. The overwhelming 95% take-up rate reflects the trust homebuyers have placed in our commitment to quality, innovative layout concepts, and timely delivery.\n\"We designed Ayanna Resort Residences with the warmth of Malaysian community living in mind, blending resort-style leisure with sustainable design and nature-inspired landscapes. As we celebrate this topping-out milestone today, we remain firmly committed to delivering a vibrant, sustainable sanctuary that families can proudly call home for generations to come,” Chang added.\nRedefining High-Rise Living\nReimagining the cherished Malaysian community padang—a communal space where residents of all generations can gather, socialise, and bond—the master-planned development introduces a dynamic 1.3-acre recreational park as its centrepiece. Complete with an interactive water stream, lush tropical landscaping, and dedicated wellness facilities, this resort-inspired sanctuary offers an elevated lifestyle for multi-generational families right at home.\nComplementing its expansive lifestyle offerings, Ayanna Resort Residences incorporates the innovative \"Semi-D in the Sky\" concept, designed to address the typical compromises of high-rise living by emulating landed semi-detached homes. This layout features extended outer perimeter walls and strategically positioned corner openings—a design advantage absent in standard high-rise units—that allow abundant natural daylight and continuous airflow, creating well-ventilated living spaces and enhancing residential privacy.\nNext Steps and Future Outlook\nFollowing the completion of structural works, construction focus now shifts to architectural façade installation, exterior envelope finishing, electrical and mechanical (M&E) fittings, and interior unit fit-outs. In tandem, landscape construction across the 1.3-acre recreational park and interactive stream hub will also commence.\nCHGP remains steadfast in upholding rigorous quality control and safety standards as the project moves steadily toward completion and unit handover in Q2 2027.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAyanna Residences Bukit Jalil by Chin Hin (https://ayannaresidence.com/)\nciteturn371search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; Image: Ayanna Resort Residences Bukit Jalil by Chin Hin 1 ... Ayanna Resort Residence Bukit Jalil celebrates the harmony between lush greenery and contemporary living, offering an oasis of serenity amidst the bustling cityscape. ... Completion  | Q4 2027 ... Total Unit (824)  | Tower A: 333 Units Tower B: 491 Units\nHomes Tailored to Multigenerational Needs\n\n## Exclusive Resort-style Living\n\nImmerse yourself in a symphony of connections, where nature embraces you in its tranquil embrace. Ayanna Resort Residence Bukit Jalil celebrates the harmony between lush greenery and contemporary living, offering an oasis of serenity amidst the bustling cityscape. Step into a world where every moment is adorned with breathtaking natural beauty.\n\nDiscover the ultimate location for your lifestyle. Ideally situated between Bukit Jalil and Old Klang Road, Ayanna Resort Residence Bukit Jalil places you at the heart of convenience and excitement. Explore a myriad of lifestyle amenities, from trendy shopping destinations to world-class dining options, all just a stone’s throw away. Experience the utmost convenience as educational institutions and essential services cater to your every need.\n\n###### Kitchen Fitted by Signature Kitchen\n\n###### Spacious Units 1,155 sqft to 2,453 sqft\n\n###### 3 – 4 Bedrooms\n\n###### 1.3 Acre Recreational Park\n\nImage: Ayanna Resort Residences Bukit Jalil by Chin Hin 3\n\nGet VVIP 